 "signs": [
  {
   "x": 30,
   "y": 17,
   "text": "THE ENCLOSURE GIFT SHOP. Authentic Dragon Scales, 3 for 2! Small print: crisps. Salt and vinegar. Ingredients: potato."
  },
  {
   "x": 21,
   "y": 25,
   "text": "THE THIRTY-NINE STEPS. Down to the cathedral. Up again is the part nobody mentions."
  },
  {
   "x": 20,
   "y": 19,
   "text": "ST DAVIDS. Population about 1,600. A city because of the cathedral. Pop in. They'll pretend not to be surprised."
  },
  {
   "x": 28,
   "y": 35,
   "text": "RIVER ALUN. Shallow, polite, and the reason the cathedral sits in a hollow: nobody could see it from the sea."
  },
  {
   "x": 29,
   "y": 7,
   "text": "BLUE PLAQUE: St David, patron saint of Wales, founded a monastery here in the sixth century.",
   "kind": "plaque",
   "dx": -0.475,
   "plaque": "st_davids_dewi_sant",
   "title": "Dewi Sant"
  },
  {
   "x": 29,
   "y": 9,
   "plaque": "st_davids_st_non",
   "title": "St Non's Chapel",
   "text": "On the cliffs just south of the city stand the ruins of St Non's Chapel and her holy well. Non was David's mother, and legend says he was born there in a wild storm while the spot itself stayed bright and calm. Pilgrims still visit the well, said to help sore eyes."
  },
  {
   "x": 35,
   "y": 30,
   "plaque": "st_davids_bishops_palace",
   "title": "The Bishop's Palace",
   "text": "Much of the Bishop's Palace was built by Bishop Henry de Gower in the 1300s, for bishops who liked to entertain on a grand scale. Look for the arcaded parapet, a row of arches running along the top of the walls. It has been a ruin for centuries, but a very fancy one."
  },
  {
   "x": 10,
   "y": 32,
   "plaque": "st_davids_little_things",
   "title": "Do the Little Things",
   "text": "Dewi Sant's last sermon is remembered as 'Byddwch lawen, cadwch y ffydd, a gwnewch y pethau bychain': be joyful, keep the faith, and do the little things. It is still a much loved Welsh saying. Today that might mean leaving someone the last Welsh cake."
  },
  {
   "x": 38,
   "y": 16,
   "plaque": "st_davids_gerald",
   "title": "Gerald of Wales",
   "text": "Gerald of Wales, Gerallt Gymro, spent years trying to become Bishop of St Davids and never quite managed it. In 1188 he toured Wales recruiting for the Crusade and wrote it all up in his Journey Through Wales, a travel book full of gossip, miracles and beavers."
  }
 ],
